The exact verifier requires only Python >= 3.10 and the Python standard
library.  No package installation is needed.

To check the rational certificate:

    python3 scripts/verify_certificate.py

To run the smoke test:

    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests

Optional: floating-point LP search
----------------------------------

The file scripts/search_lp_certificate.py rebuilds the floating-point LP used
to search for the certificate.  This is not part of the formal proof.  It
requires scipy:

    python3 -m venv .venv
    source .venv/bin/activate
    python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
    python3 -m pip install ".[search]"
    python3 scripts/search_lp_certificate.py

The proof-relevant artifact is scripts/verify_certificate.py, which checks the
final rationalized certificate exactly over Q.
